You might want to wish for a black dragon corpse. Disintegration
resistance is worth a wish, I think.

> So, I think I must get gantlets of dexterity, but apart from
> that my armor is pretty cool. Maybe a T-shirt or a Hawaian
> shirt?

If I were you, I'd go for the T-shirt, since it's easier to spell. :-)

> I have a cloak of protection in my stash that I would like
> to wear instead of my cloak of magic resistance, so I
> would like something else that gives magic resistance,
> but I don't know if there are any articfacts I can use
> that would do that, me being chaotic...

Note that a cloak is the safest means of getting and *keeping* magic
resistance, since it won't be stolen by the Wizard.

If you don't mind becoming lawful, the Orb of Detection (archeologist
Quest artifact) will do, as would the Sceptre of Might (caveman) and the
Magic Mirror of Merlin (knight).

The Eyes of the Overworld (monk, neutral) of the Platinum Yendorian
Express Card (tourist) will also do it, but it will take more than a
helm of opposite alignment to become neutral.

By the way, note that since the Eye is normally neutral, not chaotic,
there is no chaotic Quest artifact that confers magic resistance... I
wonder whether this is by design or coincidence.

> I think I might find a wand of death handy also...

Especially in the endgame. You may wish to keep two charges for when you
get there.

